  m_text: The centre of the scene features a cylindrical mirror. Behind the mirror,
    close to the back wall, is the original object. In front of the mirror is the
    camera (point of view). The camera is positioned between the mirror and the deformed
    object. By using the "Ray Tracer" panel on the right, we can fly to the perspective
    of the camera. Through the pixel screen, we are able to see the reflection of
    the object on the mirror surface. The reflection should look similar to the original
    object, referenced behind the mirror. To see an unobstructed view of the object
    and its reflection, click on "Render image".
